  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 148 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nSome lingering showers are possible on Tuesday, otherwise a dry\nforecast is expected into Wednesday. Sunshine will be more \nprevalent Tuesday afternoon and again on Wednesday, with slightly \nwarmer temperatures. The warmest day will be Wednesday, with \nafternoon highs in the low to mid 80s. \n\nRain chances will return to the area beginning Thursday and\npersisting through Saturday. Southwest flow aloft will prevail\nthrough the period, as broad troughing develops along the West \nCoast. Several disturbances are expected to affect the region, \nalong with an increase in tropical moisture lifting north across \nMexico into Texas. The best rain chances (60%-90%) will be \nThursday into Thursday night, with medium rain chances Friday \ninto Friday night, then tapering off Saturday night into early \nSunday. Precipitable water values are progged to be 1.3 to 1.6 \ninches, which will contribute to heavy rainfall and the potential\nfor localized flooding, especially Thursday into Friday. Highs \nare expected to be in the mid 70s to lower 80s, with mild \novernight lows in the upper 50s to lower 60s through the extended \nperiod.",
